### 2. Test Objectives

The objective of this test strategy is to define the approach for testing the Vivi.lv website and to validate its functionality and usability.
The testing objectives are to:
* Verify that the system functions according to the defined requirements.
* Validate the main user journeys.
* Identify functional defects and usability issues.
* Verify a consistent user experience across the website.


### 3. Test Scope

In Scope
Testing is limited to manual testing of the Vivi.lv website through its user interface (UI). Testing focuses on the functionality and behavior available to users through the website’s graphical interface. The website is tested in Latvian (LV) only.

The following areas are included in the scope of testing:
* Public website pages
* Navigation
* Language selection
* Notifications
* News and news search
* Interactive map
* Train search
* Ticket selection
* Ticket purchase
* User authentication
* My Account
* Payment cards
* Favourite routes
* Purchase history
* Contact and support
* Accessibility
* Click-to-Call
* Security testing of authentication and access control
* Session management
* Input validation
* Sensitive information protection
* Protection against repeated unsuccessful sign-in attempts
* Account deletion access control

Out of Scope

The following testing activities are excluded from this project:
* Compatibility testing across multiple web browsers
* Advanced performance, load and stress testing
* Backend services and database testing
* Infrastructure and server performance testing
* Third-party service testing
* Penetration testing
* Automated attack testing
* Advanced Infrastructure security testing

### 4. Testing Approach

Testing will be performed using a black-box approach based on publicly available website functionality and defined user flows.

The following testing techniques will be used:
* Requirement-based testing to verify compliance with functional requirements.
* Scenario-based testing to validate end-to-end user journeys.

### 5. Test Types

Functional testing will verify that system features operate according to the defined requirements.
Examples:
* Train search
* Ticket purchase
* User account management
* News search
* Contact form submission

Non-functional testing will evaluate the system’s usability, accessibility, and other quality attributes.
Usability testing examples:
* Navigation clarity
* User interface consistency
* User interaction flow
* Error message clarity
Accessibility testing examples:
* Text size adjustment
* Colour contrast options
* Accessibility settings reset functionality

Business Rules testing will verify that the system applies the defined business rules and constraints correctly.
Examples:
* Validation of required fields
* Validation of departure and arrival station selections
* Validation of travel date selections
* Verification that ticket prices and journey details are displayed correctly

Security testing will evaluate whether the system protects user accounts, sessions, and sensitive information against unauthorised access and misuse.
Examples:
* Authentication and access control
* Session management
* Input validation
* Sensitive information protection
* Handling of repeated unsuccessful sign-in attempts
* Account deletion access control

Smoke testing will verify that the application’s critical functionality works and that the system is stable enough for further testing.
Examples:
* Opening the homepage
* Navigating to the train search page
* Performing a basic train search
* Viewing available journey details
* Accessing the sign-in page

Regression testing will verify that existing functionality continues to work as expected after code changes, bug fixes, or new features are introduced.
Examples:
* Rechecking sign-in functionality after authentication changes
* Rechecking train search after changes to search functionality
* Verifying that journey details are still displayed correctly after interface updates
* Verifying that existing navigation links still work after website updates
* Rechecking ticket purchase functionality after related changes


### 6. Test Levels

